course: dictionary
lesson: 13675
title: Inhabited and uninhabited
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Some words tell you who lives in a place. Inhabited is one of them. It means having people or animals living in it. «The island is inhabited by seals and seabirds.» Seals and birds live there, so the island is not empty.
explain: The word un- at the front means not. «The small island is uninhabited, so nobody has ever built a house there.» Uninhabited means nobody lives there. Un- is a prefix, a small part added to the start of a word to change its meaning.
explain: Inhabit is also a verb meaning to live in a place. «Dinosaurs inhabited the land millions of years ago.» Here inhabited is the past tense, so it means they lived there. Use the clues in the sentence to decide which meaning fits.
fact: Inhabited means having people or animals living in it.
fact: Inhabit is a verb that means to live in a place, and inhabited is its past form.
fact: Uninhabited means nobody lives there, because un- means not.
fact: «Densely inhabited» means many people live close together in a small area.
fact: Animals inhabit habitats, so a pond is inhabited by frogs, newts and insects.
exercise: «The small island is uninhabited, so nobody has ever built a house there.» What does uninhabited mean? | Very far away | Covered in ice | *Nobody lives there | Full of people
exercise: «Frogs and newts inhabit the pond.» Which word in the sentence means live in? | newts | frogs | *inhabit | pond
exercise: «Dinosaurs inhabited the land millions of years ago.» Did dinosaurs live on the land? | No, the land was empty | *Yes, they lived there | There are not enough clues to say | Yes, but only in the sea
test: «The city is densely inhabited, with thousands of people in every street.» What does densely inhabited mean? | Only animals live there | *Many people live close together | Nobody lives there | The city is far from the sea
test: «Bats inhabit the dark cave at night.» What do the bats do? | Sleep outside the cave | Fly over the sea | Hunt for fish in the river | *Live in the cave
exam: «The planet was inhabited by strange green creatures, so the astronauts landed carefully.» What does inhabited mean here? | Was empty and silent | Was closed to visitors | *Had creatures living on it | Was made of ice
